  "statement": "Solve the differential equation $\\dfrac{d^{2}y}{dx^{2}}-5\\dfrac{dy}{dx}+6y=0$.",
  "solution": "The auxiliary equation is $m^{2}-5m+6=0$, i.e. $(m-2)(m-3)=0$, giving roots $m=2,3$. Hence the general solution is $y=Ae^{2x}+Be^{3x}$ where $A,B$ are arbitrary constants.",
